==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Brave Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Dark Cat''' at level 20+10 using [[Cat Capsule|Cat Tickets]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Axe Cat is only useful early in the game because it is the first proper damage dealer a player obtains, as its damage output greatly exceeds that of [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], and also has higher range. This makes Axe Cat useful against the likes of [[Those Guys]], who can be a pain for newer players because of their high health and attack speed, and [[Pigge]], which Axe Cat has an advantage against, as its Strong Ability gives it higher stats versus Reds.

Unfortunately, Axe Cat soon becomes redundant as longer-ranged damage dealers like [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]] become available. While Axe Cat can still be used as a supplementary source of damage, it is greatly hindered by its horrible stats for its very high cost, to the point where it simply isn't worth using. The misery for Axe Cat only continues when stronger attackers and anti-Red specialists like [[Crazed Axe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Axe Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]] are unlocked, as they all easily outclass it in some manner. Axe, however, is still a serviceable combo slave for players who do not have access to better equivalents.

==='''True Form'''===
Dark Cat has double the base stats of his previous forms, though much like how Cat's stat bonuses in True Form contribute little, Dark Cat still isn't viable as an attacker.

However, Dark Cat does gain a Weaken Effect UP [[Cat Combo]] with Dark Lazer, namely [[Power of Darkness (Combo)|Power of Darkness]]. This is especially helpful when used in tandem with [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Onmyoji Cat]] or [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]] by extending their Weaken Uptime, thereby greatly improving their effectiveness in action.

