==Trivia==
*In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], Axe Cat costs 2,000 [[XP Function|XP]] to unlock instead of 0.
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.4 Update|Version 2.0.4]] reduced Dark Cat's base health from 600 to 400 and base attack from 75 to 50, and increased base recharge from 210f<sup>7s</sup> to 300f<sup>10s</sup>.
*Brave Cat's design and description is a reference to the [[Wikipedia:Hero (Dragon Quest III)|Hero]] from [[Wikipedia:Dragon Quest III|Dragon Quest III]].
**The Combo [[Playing Slayer (Combo)|Playing Slayer]] further plays into this.
*Dark Cat's description may be a reference to [[Wikipedia:Batman|Batman]], i.e., The Dark Knight.
*Axe Cat's icon in the [[Upgrade Menu]] shows him with a brown axe handle, but in [[Battle]], his icon shows him with a grey axe handle.
**Brave Cat is shown as grey in both icons, he just has a brown filter over his icon.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Brave Cat was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Cat Army MkII (Removed Combo)|Cat Army MkII]] and [[Maxed Out (Removed Combo)|Maxed Out]].
*[[Berserkory]]'s axe looks the same as Axe Cat's, only Berserkory's is bloodstained.
**In his Japanese description, it's Axe Cat whose house he was freeloading at. Additionally, Axe Cat's Japanese name is Battle Cat while Berserkory's is Battle Koalakkyo.
*The cross on Brave Cat's shield could be a reference to the [[wikipedia:Crusades#Ideology|Crusaders]], although it is also likely just an indication of the shape of the shield.
*Prior to [[Version 15.5 Update|Version 15.5]], Axe Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Axe Cat
Combat maniac.
Strong against red enemies.</pre>
<pre>Brave Cat
Hero wannabe.
Strong against red enemies. </pre>
<pre>Dark Cat
Dark Knight wannabe
Decent Battle Cat
Strong against red enemies. </pre>

